# the planner's search (CellPlan.xtl, cp:b_uild) on nets/blinker.net: the
# program it writes, which must be programs/blinker.cell (the golden
# cell-plan-blinker); every step tried on the simulator, the refusals
# kept as comments
"cp:" u_se< "CellPlan"
cp:b_uild "# blinker: the 555 LED blinker (circuits/blinker.toml), for the planner's\n# search (CellPlan.xtl, cp:b_uild): the core, then each net and the pins\n# it joins. The planner places the core legs up, joins the core's pins\n# that share a net, lays a lead of each other part alongside its pin,\n# finishes each part's other leads as soon as it is soldered, and tries\n# each step on the simulator, keeping the first that it takes.\ncircuit blinker\ncore U1 dip8\nnet VCC U1.8 U1.4 R1.1 BT1.1\nnet DIS U1.7 R1.2 R2.1\nnet THR U1.6 U1.2 R2.2 C1.1\nnet CTRL U1.5 C2.1\nnet OUT U1.3 R3.1\nnet LED R3.2 D1.1\nnet GND U1.1 C1.2 C2.2 D1.2 BT1.2\n"
